#: manual/api/container.md:1
msgid "container API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:3
msgid "`Luna-Flow/linear-algebra/container` describes how generic code observes, builds and edits linear containers without knowing their storage. A capability is an *operation dictionary*: a record of functions for one container type `V` or `M` and one element type `T`. Five generic algorithms (map, convert and transpose) are written against these dictionaries. Ready-made dictionaries for the repository's own types are in [`container/adapters`](container/adapters.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:10
msgid "Source: [`src/container/vector_ops.mbt`](../../../src/container/vector_ops.mbt), [`src/container/matrix_ops.mbt`](../../../src/container/matrix_ops.mbt), [`src/container/generic_algorithms.mbt`](../../../src/container/generic_algorithms.mbt). The model is explained in the [container design](../design/container.md); the [integration guide](../integration/container.md) shows how external libraries publish dictionaries."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:17
msgid "[!WARNING] `container` is experimental. Record fields, error contracts and algorithm signatures may change incompatibly before the package is declared stable."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:32
msgid "Contracts shared by all dictionaries"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:34
msgid "Every function in a dictionary is checked: it returns a `Result` and must not abort for any argument."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:37
msgid "A read or edit at an index outside the shape returns an error of kind `IndexOutOfBounds`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:39
msgid "A build with a negative length or dimension returns an error of kind `NegativeDimension` and does not call the initializer."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:41
msgid "Degenerate shapes $0 \\times n$ and $n \\times 0$ are valid and must be preserved exactly; they are not the same as $0 \\times 0$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:43
msgid "Matrix coordinates are `(row, col)`, zero-based. Builders call the initializer with `(row, col)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:46
msgid "The record fields are public and readable. Call a field as a function with parentheses around the field access: `(ops.get)(m, 0, 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:49
msgid "Vector dictionaries"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:53
msgid "`VectorReadOps[V, T]` observes a vector-like container `V` with elements `T`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:62
msgid "`length(v)` returns the number of elements $n \\ge 0$; `get(v, i)` returns element $i$ for $0 \\le i < n$ and `IndexOutOfBounds` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:67
msgid "`VectorReadOps::new(length, get)` builds a read dictionary from two functions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:75
msgid "`VectorBuildOps[V, T]` constructs vectors of type `V` from an index function."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:83
msgid "`tabulate(n, f)` returns the vector $(f(0), \\dots, f(n-1))$, or `NegativeDimension` for $n < 0$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:88
msgid "`VectorBuildOps::new(tabulate)` builds a build dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:96
msgid "`VectorPersistentEditOps[V, T]` replaces one element and returns a new value."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:104
msgid "`set(v, i, x)` returns a vector equal to `v` except at index $i$, where it holds `x`. The argument `v` must remain unchanged, even if the implementation shares storage between versions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:110
msgid "`VectorPersistentEditOps::new(set)` builds a persistent-edit dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:118
msgid "`VectorMutableEditOps[V, T]` replaces one element in place."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:126
msgid "`set(v, i, x)` writes `x` at index $i$ of `v`. On error nothing is written."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/container.md:130
msgid "`VectorMutableEditOps::new(set)` builds a mutable-edit dictionary."
msgstr ""

