msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:162
msgid "**Avoiding copies.** `Matrix::from_array` and `Vector::from_array` adopt the array you pass. This is fast but means the array and the matrix change together; call `copy()` when you need independence."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:166
msgid "**Transpose without copying.** `to_transpose()` is an $O(1)$ view; products of two views reuse the matrix kernel. Use `transpose()` or `materialize()` when you need an independent matrix."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:170
msgid "**Unchecked forms in hot loops.** After you have established the preconditions (for example square matrices built by your own code), the `unchecked_*` methods skip validation. Never use `unchecked_matmul` on shapes you have not checked: it does not validate and may return a wrong result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:175
msgid "**Scaling.** The routines decide \"zero\" with an absolute threshold of $10^{-11}$. Scale your data to order one first; otherwise tiny but regular matrices are reported singular. See the [design page](../design/mutable.md#tolerance-based-decisions)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:180
msgid "**Generic code.** Wrap the matrix in `@default.DenseMatrix` to pass it to functions bounded by the `algebra` traits; `inner()` gets it back."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:185
msgid "**Forgetting that `reduce_row_elimination` mutates.** It transforms the receiver in place and returns it. Call `copy()` first."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:187
msgid "**Expecting normalized $2 \\times 2$ eigenvectors.** For $2 \\times 2$ input, the eigenvector columns are not normalized; larger inputs return orthonormal columns."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:190
msgid "**Numerical routines on integers.** `determinant`, `inverse`, `rank`, `eigen` and friends need `Tolerance`, which exists only for `Float` and `Double`. For exact integer determinants use `@immut.Matrix::determinant`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:193
msgid "**`Float` precision.** The tolerance is far below `Float` precision; nearly singular `Float` matrices are not detected. Prefer `Double`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/mutable.md:195
msgid "**Power method on symmetric spectra.** Eigenvalues $\\pm\\lambda$ of equal magnitude prevent convergence; `power_method` then returns `None`."
msgstr ""

